  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1217 AM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nLow to medium rain chances continue Thursday night into Friday \nwith a boundary in the area. There may be lesser coverage in any \nshowers or thunderstorms Friday due to the slight eastward \nprogression of the mid-level ridge during the day. High \ntemperatures relax slightly Friday into the weekend though the mid\n90s to around 103 degrees will still be common each day depending\non location. An increase in moisture will bump up heat index \nvalues, however, so there may be a need for additional heat \nproducts but confidence is low at this time. Weak ridging this \nweekend is interrupted by a disturbance moving towards the Gulf \ncoast early next week. This could bring back some low rain chances\nto the area and keep highs below Heat Advisory levels.",
